# Reversal

The Reversal API lets you reverse a completed Customer-to-Business (C2B) transaction. The request is processed asynchronously and the result is delivered to your `ResultURL` as a callback.

## How It Works

1. Your application sends a reversal request to the API.
2. The API processes the reversal and reverses the funds.
3. The result is posted to the callback URL you provided.

## Authentication

You need a valid [access token](/info/daraja-auth) and a [security credential](/info/security-credential) generated from the initiator's password.

## Request

```http
POST /mpesa/reversal/v1/request
```

### Request Body

```json
{
  "Initiator": "test_initiator",
  "SecurityCredential": "jUb+dOXJiBDui8FnruaFckZJQup3kmmCH5XJ4NY/Oo3KaUTmJbxUiVgzBjqdL533u5Q435MT2VJwr/1fuZvA===",
  "CommandID": "TransactionReversal",
  "TransactionID": "PDU91HIVIT",
  "Amount": "200",
  "ReceiverParty": "603021",
  "RecieverIdentifierType": "11",
  "ResultURL": "https://mydomain.com/reversal/result",
  "QueueTimeOutURL": "https://mydomain.com/reversal/queue",
  "Remarks": "Payment reversal"
}
```

### Request Parameters

| Field | Description | Type | Required | Example |
|-------|-------------|------|----------|---------|
| `Initiator` | Username of the API user | String | Yes | `johndoe` |
| `SecurityCredential` | Encrypted initiator password | String | Yes | `RC6E9WDx9X2c6z3gp0oC5Th==` |
| `CommandID` | Must be `TransactionReversal` | String | Yes | `TransactionReversal` |
| `Amount` | Amount to reverse | Numeric | Yes | `100` |
| `ReceiverParty` | Organization short code | Numeric | Yes | `600997` |
| `RecieverIdentifierType` | Organization type (`11` for short code) | Numeric | Yes | `11` |
| `Remarks` | Note (2–100 characters) | String | Yes | Any string |
| `QueueTimeOutURL` | Timeout notification URL | URL | Yes | `https://mydomain.com/reversal/timedout` |
| `ResultURL` | Result notification URL | URL | Yes | `https://mydomain.com/reversal/result` |
| `TransactionID` | Receipt of the transaction to reverse | String | Yes | `PDU91HIVIT` |

## Synchronous Response

A valid request receives an immediate acknowledgement.

```json
{
  "OriginatorConversationID": "f1e2-4b95-a71d-b30d3cdbb7a7735297",
  "ConversationID": "AG_20210706_20106e9209f64bebd05b",
  "ResponseCode": "0",
  "ResponseDescription": "Accept the service request successfully."
}
```

| Field | Description | Example |
|-------|-------------|---------|
| `ConversationID` | Unique identifier for this request | `4f31-fd2d5deb744c` |
| `OriginatorConversationID` | Unique identifier from M-PESA | `AG_20210706_2010ead4245` |
| `ResponseCode` | `0` = accepted | `0` |
| `ResponseDescription` | Acknowledgement message | `Accept the service request successfully.` |

## Callback

The result is posted to your `ResultURL` once processing is complete.

### Successful

```json
{
  "Result": {
    "ResultType": 0,
    "ResultCode": 0,
    "ResultDesc": "The service request is processed successfully.",
    "OriginatorConversationID": "dad6-4c34-8787-c8cb963a496d1268232",
    "ConversationID": "AG_20211114_201018edbbf9f1582eaa",
    "TransactionID": "SKE52PAWR9",
    "ResultParameters": {
      "ResultParameter": [
        { "Key": "DebitAccountBalance", "Value": "Utility Account|KES|7722179.62|7722179.62|0.00|0.00" },
        { "Key": "Amount", "Value": 1.0 },
        { "Key": "TransCompletedTime", "Value": 20211114132711 },
        { "Key": "OriginalTransactionID", "Value": "SKC82PACB8" },
        { "Key": "Charge", "Value": 0.0 },
        { "Key": "CreditPartyPublicName", "Value": "254705912645 - NICHOLAS JOHN SONGOK" },
        { "Key": "DebitPartyPublicName", "Value": "600992 - Safaricom Daraja 992" }
      ]
    },
    "ReferenceData": {
      "ReferenceItem": {
        "Key": "QueueTimeoutURL",
        "Value": "https://internalsandbox.safaricom.co.ke/mpesa/reversalresults/v1/submit"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Unsuccessful

```json
{
  "Result": {
    "ResultType": 0,
    "ResultCode": "R000002",
    "ResultDesc": "The OriginalTransactionID is invalid.",
    "OriginatorConversationID": "3124-481d-b706-10bdd6fbc8e21792398",
    "ConversationID": "AG_20211114_2010573069aefb6b625a",
    "TransactionID": "SKE0000000",
    "ReferenceData": {
      "ReferenceItem": {
        "Key": "QueueTimeoutURL",
        "Value": "https://internalsandbox.safaricom.co.ke/mpesa/reversalresults/v1/submit"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Callback Parameters

| Field | Description | Type | Optional |
|-------|-------------|------|----------|
| `Result` | Root wrapper for the result | JSON Object | No |
| `ResultType` | Always `0` | Numeric | No |
| `ResultCode` | `0` = success, otherwise see codes below | String | No |
| `ResultDesc` | Outcome description | String | No |
| `OriginatorConversationID` | Unique ID from the reversal request | String | No |
| `ConversationID` | Unique ID from M-PESA | String | No |
| `TransactionID` | Receipt for the reversal | String | No |
| `ResultParameters` | Extra transaction details | JSON Object | Yes |
| `DebitAccountBalance` | Remaining balances | String | Yes |
| `Amount` | Reversed amount | Decimal | Yes |
| `TransCompletedTime` | Completion time (`YYYYMMDDhhmmss`) | String | Yes |
| `OriginalTransactionID` | Receipt of the reversed transaction | String | Yes |
| `Charge` | Fee charged | String | Yes |
| `CreditPartyPublicName` | Refund recipient name | String | Yes |
| `DebitPartyPublicName` | Debited organization name | String | Yes |
| `ReferenceData` | Reference metadata | JSON Object | Yes |

## Result Codes

| Code | Description | Explanation |
|------|-------------|-------------|
| `0` | Success | Reversal processed successfully. |
| `R000001` | Already reversed | The transaction has already been reversed. |
| `R000002` | Invalid TransactionID | The receipt number does not exist. |
| `1` | Insufficient balance | Short code lacks funds for the refund. |
| `11` | DebitParty invalid state | Organization account is not active. |
| `21` | Initiator not allowed | API user lacks the reversal role. |
| `2001` | Invalid initiator info | API user credentials are incorrect. |
| `2006` | Declined due to account rule | Organization account has restrictions. |
| `2028` | Not permitted per product assignment | Short code cannot perform reversals. |
| `8006` | Security credential locked | API user password is locked. |

## Error Responses

If the request itself is malformed, the API returns an HTTP error.

```json
{
  "requestId": "94fc-460e-a970-797968bf6a851272619",
  "errorCode": "400.002.02",
  "errorMessage": "Bad Request - Invalid TransactionID"
}
```

| Code | Message | Cause |
|------|---------|-------|
| `400.002.02` | Bad Request – Invalid XXXX | Request payload does not match the schema. |
| `404.001.01` | Resource not found | Wrong endpoint URL. |
| `404.001.03` | Invalid Access Token | Token is expired or invalid. |
| `500.001.1001` | Internal Server Error | Unexpected server error. |

## Testing Notes

- Use a completed transaction (e.g. from [B2C](/info/b2c) or [STK Push](/info/stk-push)) as the reversal target.
- Reversing the same transaction twice returns `R000001`.
- A non-existent receipt number returns `R000002`.
- An incorrect initiator password returns `2001`.
